# Build context exclusions.
#
# The first entry is the load-bearing one. Both Dockerfiles copy `packages/` and
# an app directory wholesale after `pnpm install` has already run in the image,
# and pnpm's node_modules is a farm of symlinks into a content-addressed store
# that exists only on the machine that created it. Copying the host's copy in
# would overwrite a valid install with dangling links, and the failure surfaces
# much later as an unresolvable import.
**/node_modules

# Build output. Stale artefacts from a developer's machine must never be able to
# reach a published image — an image is supposed to contain what this build
# produced, not what somebody's laptop had lying around.
**/dist
**/.next
**/.turbo
**/out
**/build
**/coverage
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# History and local tooling.
.git
.github
.vscode
.idea
**/.DS_Store
**/*.log

# Local environment files. `.env.example` is deliberately still allowed through;
# anything else with a real value in it does not belong in an image layer.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example

# Not needed to build or run any service.
docs
infra
scripts
docker-compose.yml
enclii.yaml
**/*.md
